 "formula_en": "<p>Addition of the selected points; points assigned below. If score is &lt;16, patient can be evaluated in the &ldquo;low risk&rdquo; group with non-ischemic ECG and negative 0-hr and 2-hr troponins. These patients with these two additional features are low-risk for major adverse cardiac event.</p>\n<p>If score is &ge;16 or ECG shows new ischemia or 0-hr troponin is negative, then the patient is not low-risk and not appropriate for early discharge (obviously if the first troponin is negative and the patient is in the low-risk group, but the second troponin is positive, this patient no longer qualifies as low-risk).</p>\n<p>A negative ECG is defined as the absence of new or concerning signs of ischemia, including ST-segment elevation or depression, T-wave inversion, or other pathologic changes suggestive of ischemia or myocardial injury.</p>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<table><colgroup><col width=\"415\"><col width=\"156\"><col width=\"52\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Variable</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Points</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"10\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Age</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">18-45</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">46-50</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">51-55</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">6</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">56-60</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">8</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">61-65</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">10</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">66-70</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">12</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">71-75</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">14</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">76-80</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">16</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">81-85</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">18</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&ge;86</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">20</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Sex</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Female</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Male</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">6</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Known coronary artery disease or &ge;3 risk factors*</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">No</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Yes</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Symptoms and signs</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Diaphoresis</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">No</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Yes</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">3</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Pain radiates to arm, shoulder, neck, or jaw</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">No</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Yes</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">5</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Pain occurred or worsened with inspiration</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">No</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Yes</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">-4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Pain is reproduced by palpation</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">No</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">0</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Yes</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">-6</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>*<a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24428678\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Than et al.</a> define coronary artery disease (CAD) as &ldquo;previous acute myocardial infarction, coronary artery bypass graft, or percutaneous intervention.&rdquo; Risk factors include dislipidaemia, diabetes, hypertension, current smoker, and family history of premature CAD. The risk factors only apply to patients 18-50.</p>\n<p></p>"
